Plan D (future) = make the framework (ies-auto-mibs) an AgentX **subagent** instead of an in-process snmpd dlmod; before that, ies-auto-mibs will first be split into a shared library so everything can see it. Question verified 2026-07-01: **is any OID data trapped inside an individual daemon (which would force that daemon to also be a subagent)?** Answer: **No — two subagents (ISS + app_moxa_framework) suffice.**

Evidence (traced the SNMP GET handler `mox_snmp_handle_entry` methods 1–4 + daemon side):
- All ies-auto-mibs OIDs register with handler `mox_snmp_handle_entry`; its data sources are ONLY: (1a) `getEntryValue_uriScalar{Config,Status}_*` → `MOXA_SNMP_{CONFIG,STATUS}_URI` → LibFrameworkUri (= **framework** config/status layer); (1b) `getEntryValue_issScalarEntry` → `LibUtil_ExecShCmd(MOXA_SNMP_URI_CTRL_CLIENT --type read --uri…)` (= **ISS** via uri-control-client); (1c) `getEntryValue_generalInfo_*` (MAC/serial/model/portNum) → `LibSystem_*` (in-process shared lib, reads EEPROM/file); (2) `entry_handle_generate_uri_value_file` → framework; (3) `entry_handle_generate_iss_value_file` → ISS. (4) dlmod = **CORRECTION 2026-07-08: earlier "not used" was WRONG — I only checked plugin_moxa_snmp.** There are ~20+ dlmod plugins in OTHER packages, each shipping a `.conf` to `/etc/moxa/netsnmp/config/` that dlmod-loads a `.so` into snmpd, all built on shared `lib_moxa_snmp_plugin` (src/handler/{scalar,table}.c): system_information (config+status), ptp (moxa_1588/moxa_ptp/iec61850/c37_238/ptpbase=5), fiber_check(+event), profinet, dhcp_relay, common_system_event, ui_service_management, iec62439_2, arp_table, dai, config_encryption, utilization, trusted_access, relay, locator, email, … **GOOD NEWS: these dlmod plugins ALL read via `LibFrameworkUri_GetUri` (framework config/status layer) — same backend as ies-auto-mibs, NOT their own daemon/SHM (a few also touch /run/auto_mibs).** So they ARE reachable by the framework broad subagent; convergence = framework subagent serves them in-process + remove the dlmod `.conf`. The "no separate daemon is a subagent" claim stays true; only "method 4 unused" was the error.
- Whole-tree scan of every `getEntryValue_*`: only `LibFrameworkUri_* / LibSystem_* / URI_CTRL_CLIENT` appear — **zero** `socket()/shm_open/shmget/connect()//var/run/…` → no getter talks to a daemon directly.
- `grep agentx|netsnmp_register|SNMPRegisterMib|init_agent` across `app_moxa_*` daemons = empty → **no non-ISS daemon registers OIDs or is a subagent** (only ISS registers, via SNMPRegisterMibWithLock).

Semantics: daemon data physically lives in daemons, but daemons do NOT serve SNMP — they expose data only through the framework config/status layer (Morris layering: daemon → status/config layer → up). So framework is the single window for all non-ISS OIDs; ISS is the only other source.

**SNMPv3 stays at the master (2026-07-13):** USM (auth/priv/engine) + VACM are done entirely by snmpd master; CLI/WEB → plugin_moxa_snmp generates snmpd.conf v3 config. Subagents (ISS, framework) inherit v3 for free — never implement USM/VACM. **Gotcha:** the AgentX PDU the master forwards to a subagent carries OID + context but NOT `securityName` (`agentx_master_handler` in net-snmp master.c). The current in-master ies-auto-mibs reads `reqinfo->asp->pdu->securityName` to map a v3 rwuser → per-user token (`rwuser_list`→`security_tokens`) for config-layer perms; a subagent loses this → per-v3-user config permissions break. Plan D B Task 5 must pick: (a) single internal identity (recommended; VACM still gates RO/RW), (b) keep v3-user-sensitive OIDs on master, (c) carry identity down (non-standard). Also: `MoxaAgentX_SendTrap` dropped — traps are out-of-band (app events → MQTT → trap_notification → /bin/snmptrap); subagent is GET/SET only.

**Why:** determines Plan D scope — no need to make each daemon a subagent; ISS + framework cover everything.
**How to apply:** Plan D framework-subagent must retain LibFrameworkUri (config/status layer) + LibSystem + uri-control-client (inherent — it IS the framework). **Design constraint to enforce:** any NEW SNMP OID must read via the config/status layer, never directly from a daemon socket/shm — else the "2 subagents suffice" invariant breaks. Note: the framework/URI path is the ~600ms slow path; Plan D is an architecture/layering win, not a perf win (perf still bounded by the config/status layer). Related: [[project-plan-c-agentx-set-path-and-framing]]. Caveat also noted there: the in-process ifAdminStatus/ifXTable GET-forward (netsnmp_call_handlers to ISS's in-master reg) only works while framework is an in-process dlmod; moving to a subagent breaks it and reopens the RW GET-fast/SET-clean split.
